VC-20 core: vendored from VIC20Nano. The partial bitstream of this core is published as a `.cor` together with this
source; no ROM is in this repository.
Rights holders who see a problem with any part listed here: please contact us, and we remove the part concerned.

Three of the files below carry additional restrictions that are not GPL compatible. Their
headers are kept as they came; the clauses are

  m6561.vhd, vic20.vhd, vic20_clocks.vhd
      (c) 2003-2009 MikeJ (FPGAArcade), (c) 2011-2015 WoS (Wolfgang Scherr):
      "any commercial use is forbidden as well. This code must be run on Replay hardware only."

What is here, and where it comes from. Upstream: https://github.com/MiSTle-Dev/VIC20Nano
(commit 9089828d8a21ea3075c0df9c87418b42766ab289, 2026-03-21), GPL-3.0 as a repository; the
files' own headers decide, not the repository licence.

  src/m6561.vhd        6561 VIC (MikeJ/WoS, voices after Viznut/pwp and Lance Ewing).
                       Changed: output O_COLOUR (the colour index behind O_VIDEO_*).
  src/vic20.vhd        the machine (MikeJ/WoS). Changed: memories are vc20_ram (inferred block RAM,
                       host window as second port) instead of the Gowin blocks and ram_conf_*;
                       ports: host window conf_*, RESTORE, O_COLOUR, O_CADDR; the PS/2 key input, the
                       Gowin CLKDIV component and the rom_std input are removed; entity via6522
                       renamed vc20_via6522.
  src/vic20_clocks.vhd clock enable and reset delay (MikeJ/WoS). Changed: initial value of div_cnt
                       (simulation only; the FPGA starts at 0).
  src/vc20_via6522.vhd 6522 VIA, Gideon Zweijtzer, GPL 3.0 ("Free to use, distribute and change").
                       Renamed from via6522 (our drive carries Gideon's 1541 via6522 under that
                       name); content unchanged.
  src/vic20_keyboard.vhd  key matrix glue (no header; MiSTeryNano / Till Harbaum lineage), unchanged.
  src/t65/*            T65 6502 core (Daniel Wallner, 2002-2015; T65(b) fixes by FPGAARCADE, WoS,
                       SzGy), BSD-style header, unchanged.

Not taken from upstream: the Gowin primitives and IP, ram_conf_*.vhd (Wolfgang Scherr, "only
allowed on Replay hardware"), the loader, the HDMI/OSD/MCU/SD/SDRAM parts, the c1541 (our drive_unit
is the 1541), c1530 (tape) and megacart.v (M2, later).

trx/ is ours (GPL-3.0-or-later like the rest of the project) and has no upstream code. The Commodore
ROMs (BASIC, KERNAL, CHAR) are not in the repository and not in any bitstream; the app writes them
into the machine at run time.
